{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EnHrXcEDzPKBNKHBgv9rnV","type":"tool_result","content":"205\t    resolves as infrastructure and fails open (advisory). That is\n206\t    unchanged.\n207\t  - With `--harness codex`, the installer now prints that it was verified\n208\t    against Codex CLI 0.160.0, while the hook fixtures date from 0.139.0.\n209\t\n210\t### Fixed — the kernel's hard-deny list covers the code the v1.4.4 split moved out of seven kernel entry points, five flat modules that kernel code calls, and the live-adapter package\n211\t\n212\t- The split (PLAN-197) moved the code of seven kernel entry points into\n213\t  helper packages: five hooks (canonical edit, pair rail, agent spawn,\n214\t  audit log and Bash safety) and two hook library modules (policy and\n215\t  audit emit). The same train replaced the plan-path regexes of two\n216\t  kernel files, the plan-lifecycle hook (`check_plan_edit.py`) and the\n217\t  policy preprocessors (`_lib/policy_preprocessors.py`), with the\n218\t  plan-path predicate in `_lib/plan_paths.py`. The kernel's hard-deny\n219\t  list (`check_arbitration_kernel.py`) kept naming only the kernel files,\n220\t  so the 81 files of those packages and the predicate were canonical\n221\t  only: a signed sentinel could unlock them. The list now has a row for\n222\t  each, so that code is hard-deny again, as it was inside the kernel\n223\t  files in v1.4.2.\n224\t- The list also enrolls four modules that kernel code calls, which were\n225\t  canonical only as well: `_lib/model_currency.py`, the VETO-floor\n226\t  predicate that the kernel files `agent_frontmatter.py` and\n227\t  `escalation_signals.py` now call as part of their VETO-floor check; and\n228\t  three modules this train added, `_lib/cli_currency.py` (the Codex\n229\t  payload-pin currency check, called by the pair-rail code),\n230\t  `_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py` (the indirect-execution matcher) and\n231\t  `_lib/bash_indirect_telemetry.py` (its disabled-rail telemetry), both\n232\t  called by the Bash guard's code.\n233\t- The live-adapter package (`_lib/adapters/live/`, 11 files: the ADR-040\n234\t  provider adapters, off by default), which the kernel\n235\t  `_lib/adapters/__init__.py` loads, was canonical only as well, since\n236\t  v1.0.0. It is now enrolled in the kernel, so an edit to it goes through\n237\t  the kernel override like an edit to any kernel file.\n238\t- The list now has one recursive row per package (the seven helper\n239\t  packages and `adapters/live/`), so a file added there later is a kernel\n240\t  path too, and one row for each of the five flat modules: 13 new rows,\n241\t  and 125 tracked kernel files become 222.\n242\t- A new test (`tests/test_kernel_decomposition_coverage.py`) derives from\n243\t  the code each helper package below `_lib/` that a kernel source reaches\n244\t  by an import statement or by a `/` chain of string literals, and checks\n245\t  that each one is kernel in full, with a positive control on the known\n246\t  packages. It also checks that each of the five flat modules is kernel\n247\t  and still imported by a kernel source. Dropping any one of the 13 new\n248\t  rows turns it red.\n249\t- No tag shipped the gap this train opened: none of the seven packages\n250\t  and five flat modules existed at v1.4.2 or v1.4.3-rc.1.\n251\t- The fix is a commit the maintainer signed, after review by two Claude\n252\t  refuters and Codex. No sentinel file covers it.\n253\t\n254\t### Fixed — the secret redactor's offsets after an NFKC-changing character (present since v1.0.0)\n255\t\n256\t- `scan()` in `_lib/secret_patterns.py` matched the NFKC-normalized view\n257\t  of a text but reported offsets in that view, while `redact()` and\n258\t  `scan_and_redact()` cut the original text with them. A character whose\n259\t  NFKC form has another length (an ellipsis, a ligature) before a secret\n260\t  shifted the cut, so part or all of the secret could survive next to its\n261\t  label. The Codex and Grok egress redactor (`_lib/codex_egress_redact.py`)\n262\t  uses these functions. Every release since v1.0.0 has the defect. The\n263\t  signed v1.4.0 verdict declared this defect as its condition 58.\n264\t- `scan()` now reports offsets in the text passed in. It matches that text\n265\t  and its NFKC view, maps the view's matches back, and merges overlapping\n266\t  findings into one span. The output is the original text with only those\n267\t  spans replaced; no normalized character reaches it.\n268\t- The pattern catalog is unchanged.\n269\t- The fix is a commit the maintainer signed, after review by Codex and two\n270\t  Claude refuters over several rounds.\n271\t  Codex approved it with one condition, which predates the fix and is\n272\t  declared in Known-open. No sentinel file covers it.\n273\t\n274\t### Fixed — backup and restore\n275\t\n276\t- `ceo-backup.sh` archives only the regular files of `memory/`; a link\n277\t  there is left out.\n278\t- `ceo-restore.sh`:\n279\t  - checks every archive member before extraction (`_restore_archive.py`):\n280\t    no links, no absolute paths, no `..`, no name outside the layout, and\n281\t    never `audit-key` or `.salt`, in any letter case;\n282\t  - resolves `--dest` physically and refuses a link, or a file, as the\n283\t    destination;\n284\t  - refuses a restore target that is a link or sits under one;\n285\t  - runs the same checks in the preview and in the apply.\n286\t- On macOS, the system `tar` adds a hidden AppleDouble member\n287\t  (`._<name>`) for each file or folder with extended attributes, and\n288\t  `ceo-restore.sh` refused every such archive (`archive refused path:\n289\t  ._.`). `ceo-backup.sh` no longer writes these members. For archives\n290\t  that already have them, restore skips such a member, without writing\n291\t  it, only when its matching file or folder is in the same archive; any\n292\t  other `._` member is refused. Restore now extracts only the members it\n293\t  accepted, in Python instead of with `tar -x`: a truncated or corrupt\n294\t  archive is refused before anything is written, and so is an archive\n295\t  with a sparse member or with two members of the same name.\n296\t- The disaster-recovery and incident-response guides no longer pass\n297\t  `--dry-run`, a flag the script refuses. The preview is the default, and\n298\t  `--apply` restores.\n299\t\n300\t### Fixed — `audit-verify-chain.py --strict-against-counter`\n301\t\n302\t- With the flag, every result maps to a documented exit code with a named\n303\t  reason, one JSON object under `--json`, and no traceback.\n304\t- An absent counter exits 0 and reports `chain_length_source: \"absent\"`.\n305\t  An unreadable counter exits 3.\n306\t- A file and stdin go through one strict decode, and a log that is not a\n307\t  regular file is refused.\n308\t- Without the flag, nothing changes.\n309\t\n310\t### Fixed — three findings of the v1.4.3-rc.1 re-pass\n311\t\n312\t- `diagnose-output-hook.py` can no longer write to the live audit log.\n313\t- `check-audit-real-loss.py` reports a malformed `record_id` instead of\n314\t  crashing.\n315\t- `audit_spool_state.py` and `check-audit-real-loss.py`, both read-only,\n316\t  stop writing bytecode.\n317\t\n318\t### Fixed — harness gate, root `CLAUDE.md` exclusion, plan lifecycle, cost envelope\n319\t\n320\t- `check-active-hooks-executable.py` validates a hook's `type` and\n321\t  `matcher` the way the loader does. A settings path that exists but is\n322\t  not a regular file, and a filesystem error while resolving a hook path,\n323\t  exit 2 with a named error.\n324\t- `check_harness_config.py` turns an exception in that sub-check into a\n325\t  RED finding and keeps its output. Before, it was a degraded warning,\n326\t  which reads as green.\n327\t- A `claudeMdExcludes` value that excludes the root `CLAUDE.md` is\n328\t  classified as settings tamper (`settings_tamper_claude_md_excludes_root`).\n329\t- The harness gate adds an advisory finding, `root_instruction_load`. It\n330\t  reports `root_load_unobservable` unless you pass a complete list of the\n331\t  loaded instruction files with `--instruction-load-evidence`.\n332\t- The plan-lifecycle hook recognizes `PLAN-NNN-FOLLOWUP-<slug>.md` names\n333\t  (`_lib/plan_paths.py`).\n334\t- `check_cost_envelope.py` evaluates nothing, and records no spend, without\n335\t  an absolute `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`. Before, it fell back to the current\n336\t  directory.\n337\t\n338\t### Changed — `/ceo-boot` and other files that reach installs\n339\t\n340\t- `/ceo-boot` adds `main_checkout_state`. It is yellow, never red, when the\n341\t  main checkout is off its default branch or on a detached HEAD.\n342\t- The installer copies every top-level `.claude/scripts/*.py`, so six new\n343\t  maintenance helpers reach installs: `_contamination_inventory.py`,\n344\t  `_repin_guard.py`, `_restore_archive.py`, `_subprocess_census.py`,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a4f4d70-7bb8-4cdc-868c-8f5f354648e0","uuid":"a20e3aa0-52c6-4406-9b59-557ad3a4b956","timestamp":"2026-11-15T11:01:16.339Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"    resolves as infrastructure and fails open (advisory). That is\n    unchanged.\n  - With `--harness codex`, the installer now prints that it was verified\n    against Codex CLI 0.160.0, while the hook fixtures date from 0.139.0.\n\n### Fixed — the kernel's hard-deny list covers the code the v1.4.4 split moved out of seven kernel entry points, five flat modules that kernel code calls, and the live-adapter package\n\n- The split (PLAN-197) moved the code of seven kernel entry points into\n  helper packages: five hooks (canonical edit, pair rail, agent spawn,\n  audit log and Bash safety) and two hook library modules (policy and\n  audit emit). The same train replaced the plan-path regexes of two\n  kernel files, the plan-lifecycle hook (`check_plan_edit.py`) and the\n  policy preprocessors (`_lib/policy_preprocessors.py`), with the\n  plan-path predicate in `_lib/plan_paths.py`. The kernel's hard-deny\n  list (`check_arbitration_kernel.py`) kept naming only the kernel files,\n  so the 81 files of those packages and the predicate were canonical\n  only: a signed sentinel could unlock them. The list now has a row for\n  each, so that code is hard-deny again, as it was inside the kernel\n  files in v1.4.2.\n- The list also enrolls four modules that kernel code calls, which were\n  canonical only as well: `_lib/model_currency.py`, the VETO-floor\n  predicate that the kernel files `agent_frontmatter.py` and\n  `escalation_signals.py` now call as part of their VETO-floor check; and\n  three modules this train added, `_lib/cli_currency.py` (the Codex\n  payload-pin currency check, called by the pair-rail code),\n  `_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py` (the indirect-execution matcher) and\n  `_lib/bash_indirect_telemetry.py` (its disabled-rail telemetry), both\n  called by the Bash guard's code.\n- The live-adapter package (`_lib/adapters/live/`, 11 files: the ADR-040\n  provider adapters, off by default), which the kernel\n  `_lib/adapters/__init__.py` loads, was canonical only as well, since\n  v1.0.0. It is now enrolled in the kernel, so an edit to it goes through\n  the kernel override like an edit to any kernel file.\n- The list now has one recursive row per package (the seven helper\n  packages and `adapters/live/`), so a file added there later is a kernel\n  path too, and one row for each of the five flat modules: 13 new rows,\n  and 125 tracked kernel files become 222.\n- A new test (`tests/test_kernel_decomposition_coverage.py`) derives from\n  the code each helper package below `_lib/` that a kernel source reaches\n  by an import statement or by a `/` chain of string literals, and checks\n  that each one is kernel in full, with a positive control on the known\n  packages. It also checks that each of the five flat modules is kernel\n  and still imported by a kernel source. Dropping any one of the 13 new\n  rows turns it red.\n- No tag shipped the gap this train opened: none of the seven packages\n  and five flat modules existed at v1.4.2 or v1.4.3-rc.1.\n- The fix is a commit the maintainer signed, after review by two Claude\n  refuters and Codex. No sentinel file covers it.\n\n### Fixed — the secret redactor's offsets after an NFKC-changing character (present since v1.0.0)\n\n- `scan()` in `_lib/secret_patterns.py` matched the NFKC-normalized view\n  of a text but reported offsets in that view, while `redact()` and\n  `scan_and_redact()` cut the original text with them. A character whose\n  NFKC form has another length (an ellipsis, a ligature) before a secret\n  shifted the cut, so part or all of the secret could survive next to its\n  label. The Codex and Grok egress redactor (`_lib/codex_egress_redact.py`)\n  uses these functions. Every release since v1.0.0 has the defect. The\n  signed v1.4.0 verdict declared this defect as its condition 58.\n- `scan()` now reports offsets in the text passed in. It matches that text\n  and its NFKC view, maps the view's matches back, and merges overlapping\n  findings into one span. The output is the original text with only those\n  spans replaced; no normalized character reaches it.\n- The pattern catalog is unchanged.\n- The fix is a commit the maintainer signed, after review by Codex and two\n  Claude refuters over several rounds.\n  Codex approved it with one condition, which predates the fix and is\n  declared in Known-open. No sentinel file covers it.\n\n### Fixed — backup and restore\n\n- `ceo-backup.sh` archives only the regular files of `memory/`; a link\n  there is left out.\n- `ceo-restore.sh`:\n  - checks every archive member before extraction (`_restore_archive.py`):\n    no links, no absolute paths, no `..`, no name outside the layout, and\n    never `audit-key` or `.salt`, in any letter case;\n  - resolves `--dest` physically and refuses a link, or a file, as the\n    destination;\n  - refuses a restore target that is a link or sits under one;\n  - runs the same checks in the preview and in the apply.\n- On macOS, the system `tar` adds a hidden AppleDouble member\n  (`._<name>`) for each file or folder with extended attributes, and\n  `ceo-restore.sh` refused every such archive (`archive refused path:\n  ._.`). `ceo-backup.sh` no longer writes these members. For archives\n  that already have them, restore skips such a member, without writing\n  it, only when its matching file or folder is in the same archive; any\n  other `._` member is refused. Restore now extracts only the members it\n  accepted, in Python instead of with `tar -x`: a truncated or corrupt\n  archive is refused before anything is written, and so is an archive\n  with a sparse member or with two members of the same name.\n- The disaster-recovery and incident-response guides no longer pass\n  `--dry-run`, a flag the script refuses. The preview is the default, and\n  `--apply` restores.\n\n### Fixed — `audit-verify-chain.py --strict-against-counter`\n\n- With the flag, every result maps to a documented exit code with a named\n  reason, one JSON object under `--json`, and no traceback.\n- An absent counter exits 0 and reports `chain_length_source: \"absent\"`.\n  An unreadable counter exits 3.\n- A file and stdin go through one strict decode, and a log that is not a\n  regular file is refused.\n- Without the flag, nothing changes.\n\n### Fixed — three findings of the v1.4.3-rc.1 re-pass\n\n- `diagnose-output-hook.py` can no longer write to the live audit log.\n- `check-audit-real-loss.py` reports a malformed `record_id` instead of\n  crashing.\n- `audit_spool_state.py` and `check-audit-real-loss.py`, both read-only,\n  stop writing bytecode.\n\n### Fixed — harness gate, root `CLAUDE.md` exclusion, plan lifecycle, cost envelope\n\n- `check-active-hooks-executable.py` validates a hook's `type` and\n  `matcher` the way the loader does. A settings path that exists but is\n  not a regular file, and a filesystem error while resolving a hook path,\n  exit 2 with a named error.\n- `check_harness_config.py` turns an exception in that sub-check into a\n  RED finding and keeps its output. Before, it was a degraded warning,\n  which reads as green.\n- A `claudeMdExcludes` value that excludes the root `CLAUDE.md` is\n  classified as settings tamper (`settings_tamper_claude_md_excludes_root`).\n- The harness gate adds an advisory finding, `root_instruction_load`. It\n  reports `root_load_unobservable` unless you pass a complete list of the\n  loaded instruction files with `--instruction-load-evidence`.\n- The plan-lifecycle hook recognizes `PLAN-NNN-FOLLOWUP-<slug>.md` names\n  (`_lib/plan_paths.py`).\n- `check_cost_envelope.py` evaluates nothing, and records no spend, without\n  an absolute `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`. Before, it fell back to the current\n  directory.\n\n### Changed — `/ceo-boot` and other files that reach installs\n\n- `/ceo-boot` adds `main_checkout_state`. It is yellow, never red, when the\n  main checkout is off its default branch or on a detached HEAD.\n- The installer copies every top-level `.claude/scripts/*.py`, so six new\n  maintenance helpers reach installs: `_contamination_inventory.py`,\n  `_repin_guard.py`, `_restore_archive.py`, `_subprocess_census.py`,","numLines":140,"startLine":205,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EnHrXcEDzPKBNKHBgv9rnV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
