{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JPnYKvcbZ1DSFSHJPEzbdd","type":"tool_result","content":"217:def resolve_plan_id(session_id: Optional[str] = None) -> str:\n218-    \"\"\"Return the PLAN-NNN currently scoped to the given session.\n219-\n220-    Scans ``audit-log.jsonl`` (via :func:`audit_emit.iter_events`) for\n221-    ``plan_transition`` events whose ``session_id`` matches the argument\n222-    (or ``CLAUDE_SESSION_ID`` env var if the argument is None). Returns\n223-    the ``plan_id`` of the MOST RECENT matching event.\n224-\n225-    Args:\n226-        session_id: explicit session id; if None, pulled from env.\n227-\n228-    Returns:\n229-        The canonical ``PLAN-NNN`` string.\n230-\n231-    Raises:\n232-        PlanIdDerivationError: when no session id is available, when\n233-            the audit log is empty or missing, or when no\n234-            ``plan_transition`` event for the session exists.\n235-\n236-    Notes:\n237-        - **No env-var fallback.** Consensus M2 forbids deriving plan\n238-          id from ``CEO_CURRENT_PLAN`` or similar — those are\n239-          agent-spoofable.\n240-        - \"Most recent\" is *log order*: the last matching event in\n241-          linear file order wins. Timestamps are not re-sorted because\n242-          audit-log writes are ordered by the shared filelock, and\n243-          re-sorting by ts can tie-break wrong on same-second events.\n244-        - A completed-plan session (``to_status=done``) still resolves\n245-          to that plan; scratchpad clear is an explicit call, not an\n246-          implicit consequence of a terminal transition.\n247-        - **PLAN-179 W1 US3 leaves this function unchanged.** The\n248-          session-scope fallback is a NEW path taken by the CALLER after\n249-          this raises — it is not a loosening of the refusal here. This\n250-          function still never guesses a plan id and still never accepts\n251-          one from the environment.\n252-    \"\"\"\n253-    sid = _resolve_session_id(session_id)\n254-    if not sid:\n255-        raise PlanIdDerivationError(\n256-            \"cannot derive plan_id: no session_id provided and \"\n257-            \"CLAUDE_SESSION_ID env var is unset. Ensure the hook/CLI \"\n258-            \"is running in a Claude Code session with a live session id.\"\n259-        )\n260-\n261-    last_plan_id: Optional[str] = None\n262-    seen_any_transition = False\n263-    for event in _audit_emit.iter_events(action_filter=\"plan_transition\"):\n264-        seen_any_transition = True\n265-        event_sid = str(event.get(\"session_id\") or \"\")\n266-        if event_sid != sid:\n267-            continue\n268-        pid = event.get(\"plan_id\")\n269-        if isinstance(pid, str) and pid:\n270-            last_plan_id = pid\n271-\n272-    if last_plan_id is None:\n273-        if not seen_any_transition:\n274-            raise PlanIdDerivationError(\n275-                f\"cannot derive plan_id: no plan_transition events in \"\n276-                f\"audit-log for session {sid!r}. Is the audit log empty \"\n277-                f\"or pointed at the wrong path (CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH)?\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a4f4d70-7bb8-4cdc-868c-8f5f354648e0","uuid":"5b38bbca-b128-4594-9997-75743fae67d5","timestamp":"2026-11-15T11:01:54.408Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"217:def resolve_plan_id(session_id: Optional[str] = None) -> str:\n218-    \"\"\"Return the PLAN-NNN currently scoped to the given session.\n219-\n220-    Scans ``audit-log.jsonl`` (via :func:`audit_emit.iter_events`) for\n221-    ``plan_transition`` events whose ``session_id`` matches the argument\n222-    (or ``CLAUDE_SESSION_ID`` env var if the argument is None). Returns\n223-    the ``plan_id`` of the MOST RECENT matching event.\n224-\n225-    Args:\n226-        session_id: explicit session id; if None, pulled from env.\n227-\n228-    Returns:\n