{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CKX3ATgfngRSqpYMq2Cvz3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\tr\"\"\"architect-bundle-validate.py — verify an Architect draft bundle.\n3\t\n4\tSprint 5 Phase 7. Validates the 5-file bundle the Agent Architect\n5\temits into `.claude/plans/PLAN-NNN/architect/round-1/`. Used by the\n6\t`/architect` slash command after the meta-agent returns; can be run\n7\tmanually before the Owner copies `approved.md.template` to the actual\n8\tsentinel.\n9\t\n10\t## Checks\n11\t\n12\t1. Bundle directory matches `.claude/plans/PLAN-*/architect/round-*/`.\n13\t2. All 5 required draft files present + parseable:\n14\t     - team.draft.md\n15\t     - pitfalls.draft.yaml\n16\t     - skill-selection.draft.md\n17\t     - personas.draft.md\n18\t     - rationale.md\n19\t3. `team.draft.md` contains ≥5 persona sections (`### `).\n20\t4. `pitfalls.draft.yaml` parses as YAML and has ≥10 entries under\n21\t   `pitfalls:`.\n22\t5. `skill-selection.draft.md` lists ≥3 skills (heuristic: ≥3 lines\n23\t   matching `^- \\`<id>\\``).\n24\t6. No file references real-person names (heuristic against a small\n25\t   curated deny-list of public real names — Owner-extensible).\n26\t7. No file uses paid-tier marketing language (heuristic: phrases like\n27\t   \"enterprise tier\", \"paid plan\", \"pro feature\").\n28\t\n29\t## Exit codes\n30\t\n31\t- 0 — bundle passes all checks\n32\t- 1 — one or more checks failed (reasons printed)\n33\t- 2 — fatal error (bad path, no read access)\n34\t\"\"\"\n35\t\n36\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n37\t\n38\timport argparse\n39\timport re\n40\timport sys\n41\tfrom pathlib import Path\n42\tfrom typing import List, Tuple\n43\t\n44\t# Required draft files\n45\t_REQUIRED_FILES = [\n46\t    \"team.draft.md\",\n47\t    \"pitfalls.draft.yaml\",\n48\t    \"skill-selection.draft.md\",\n49\t    \"personas.draft.md\",\n50\t    \"rationale.md\",\n51\t]\n52\t\n53\t# Bundle dir glob\n54\t_BUNDLE_PATTERN = re.compile(\n55\t    r\".*/\\.claude/plans/PLAN-\\d{3}[^/]*/architect/round-\\d+/?$\"\n56\t)\n57\t\n58\t# Real-person deny-list (curated, owner-extensible). Keep minimal —\n59\t# the goal is to catch obvious leaks, not maintain an exhaustive list.\n60\t_REAL_NAMES_DENY = {\n61\t    \"Sam Altman\",\n62\t    \"Dario Amodei\",\n63\t    \"Elon Musk\",\n64\t    \"Sundar Pichai\",\n65\t    \"Satya Nadella\",\n66\t    \"Mark Zuckerberg\",\n67\t    \"Tim Cook\",\n68\t    \"Jeff Bezos\",\n69\t    \"Andy Jassy\",\n70\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a4f4d70-7bb8-4cdc-868c-8f5f354648e0","uuid":"51694ba8-8b01-450a-a383-ed93564c85b5","timestamp":"2026-11-15T11:03:22.771Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/.claude/scripts/architect-bundle-validate.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nr\"\"\"architect-bundle-validate.py — verify an Architect draft bundle.\n\nSprint 5 Phase 7. Validates the 5-file bundle the Agent Architect\nemits into `.claude/plans/PLAN-NNN/architect/round-1/`. Used by the\n`/architect` slash command after the meta-agent returns; can be run\nmanually before the Owner copies `approved.md.template` to the actual\nsentinel.\n\n## Checks\n\n1. Bundle directory matches `.claude/plans/PLAN-*/architect/round-*/`.\n2. All 5 required draft files present + parseable:\n     - team.draft.md\n     - pitfalls.draft.yaml\n     - skill-selection.draft.md\n     - personas.draft.md\n     - rationale.md\n3. `team.draft.md` contains ≥5 persona sections (`### `).\n4. `pitfalls.draft.yaml` parses as YAML and has ≥10 entries under\n   `pitfalls:`.\n5. `skill-selection.draft.md` lists ≥3 skills (heuristic: ≥3 lines\n   matching `^- \\`<id>\\``).\n6. No file references real-person names (heuristic against a small\n   curated deny-list of public real names — Owner-extensible).\n7. No file uses paid-tier marketing language (heuristic: phrases like\n   \"enterprise tier\", \"paid plan\", \"pro feature\").\n\n## Exit codes\n\n- 0 — bundle passes all checks\n- 1 — one or more checks failed (reasons printed)\n- 2 — fatal error (bad path, no read access)\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\n# Required draft files\n_REQUIRED_FILES = [\n    \"team.draft.md\",\n    \"pitfalls.draft.yaml\",\n    \"skill-selection.draft.md\",\n    \"personas.draft.md\",\n    \"rationale.md\",\n]\n\n# Bundle dir glob\n_BUNDLE_PATTERN = re.compile(\n    r\".*/\\.claude/plans/PLAN-\\d{3}[^/]*/architect/round-\\d+/?$\"\n)\n\n# Real-person deny-list (curated, owner-extensible). Keep minimal —\n# the goal is to catch obvious leaks, not maintain an exhaustive list.\n_REAL_NAMES_DENY = {\n    \"Sam Altman\",\n    \"Dario Amodei\",\n    \"Elon Musk\",\n    \"Sundar Pichai\",\n    \"Satya Nadella\",\n    \"Mark Zuckerberg\",\n    \"Tim Cook\",\n    \"Jeff Bezos\",\n    \"Andy Jassy\",\n}","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":228}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CKX3ATgfngRSqpYMq2Cvz3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
