ib and tempfile are imported inside the functions.\n  - The exception classes are the same objects as before. The facade's own _invoke_codex_review replaces part_02's identical copy.\n- _precompact_parts.install exec's each part into the facade's namespace, so name lookup matches the old single file. I spot-checked the critical lines: --first-parent, the 1.0s index share, the O_NOFOLLOW ledger chain, the bytes store path after field redaction, set_session_value, and the GC TTL.\n- Fail direction:\n  - An ImportError at the top of the facade makes Python exit 1. On the Claude Code and Codex path, _python-hook.sh `exec`s the hook (line 416), so the session is not blocked: infrastructure failure stays fail-open.\n  - On `--verify-codex-pin`, exit 1 reads as fail-closed. That is acceptable for a release gate.\n- Install: install_lib_selective (scripts/install.sh:1520-1550) copies each _lib entry, directories included, and the exclusion predicate does not match the new packages, so they ship.\n- Adopters are not affected by the pin: the pin manifest is not installed to them, so the pair rail resolves `manifest_unreadable` → infra → advisory, and the currency arm never runs there.\n- plan_paths change, declared in CHANGELOG [1.4.4] line 332:\n  - Wider: now matches FOLLOWUP names and Windows separators.\n  - Narrower: no longer matches double or trailing hyphens, or non-ASCII digits. Real plan files never use these.\n- New scripts: stdlib only and Python 3.9 compatible.\n  - _restore_archive.py writes only below a real stage directory, with O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW and the mode masked to 0o777.\n  - It refuses link, device and sparse members, duplicate names, traversal and the key files in any letter case (casefold).\n  - It requires an end-of-archive block and reads the gzip stream to its end.\n  - ceo-restore.sh runs it inside a mktemp stage with an EXIT trap. The archive directory has no stdlib-shadowing modules.\n- _repin_guard.py: the paths it writes into the shell guard are validated by _PACK_DIR_RE (re-pin-codex.py:2045). When grep returns 2 the guard stops (fail-closed).\n- architect-bundle-validate.py: the r\"\"\" change is cosmetic. \"\\`\" was an invalid escape, and the rendered text is the same.\n\nP0: none.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none at P1.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n1. P2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/plan_paths.py:26-34, used by check_plan_edit.py:151-171 and :530.\n   - Problem: plan_id_from_path returns filename[:8], so `PLAN-194-FOLLOWUP-v1-4-4-backlog.md` (frontmatter id `PLAN-194-FOLLOWUP-v1-4-4-backlog`) gives `PLAN-194`.\n   - Scenario: now that FOLLOWUP files pass is_plan_path, a status change on a followup emits a signed `plan_transition` with plan_id=PLAN-194, the parent. Metrics, dashboards and success receipts may then show the parent re-opening after `done`. detect_stranded also reports a stranded followup as its parent. Session scoping is not affected: the event carries session_id=\"\".\n   - Fix: return the full FOLLOWUP id, or take it from frontmatter `id`, or skip the transition emit for FOLLOWUP names until the event schema accepts that id shape. Say in the CHANGELOG which one was chosen.\n2. P2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_pair_rail_parts/part_01.py:477-486, with the docstrings at :394-424 and :574-575.\n   - Problem: when the host triple is absent from the manifest (every host except aarch64-apple-darwin), the currency arm runs before the override-existence check.\n   - Scenario: set CEO_PAIR_RAIL_CODEX_BIN to a missing path under a tree whose ancestor holds an `@openai/codex` package.json newer than 0.160.0. The result is `compatible` with a path that does not exist, then exec fails, then CodexUnavailable, then an advisory allow. The docstring says such an override BLOCKS (H1).\n   - Also: without an override this arm returns the npm JS launcher as the exec target, but _resolve_codex_bin says \"native payload\".\n   - Security impact is nil, since whoever controls the env can set CEO_PAIR_RAIL_DISABLE.\n   - Fix: check that the override is a regular file before the currency call, and update both docstrings.\n3. P2 — documentation honesty after the `compatible` arm.\n   - part_04.py:499 says \"0 — verified (payload sha256 matches)\", but `compatible` also exits 0.\n   - The verify_codex_payload status list (part_01.py:412) omits `compatible`, and its text still says \"No env relaxes this comparison\".\n   - The dead part_02.py:63-66 docstring still says \"the artifact that was hashed is the artifact that runs\".\n   - Fix: document `compatible` as a version-only result with no byte attestation, as C9/C10 already declare.\n4. P2 — .claude/hooks/check_pair_rail.py:21.\n   - Problem: `from _lib import cli_currency as _cli_currency  # noqa: F401` looks unused but is required: the rebound _apply_currency_policy looks _cli_currency up in the facade's globals.\n   - Scenario: a lint autofix removes the line. A sha mismatch then raises NameError inside the `except Exception → infra` handler (part_01.py:547). The result flips from mismatch (BLOCK) to infra (advisory). Any other unexpected exception in the currency arm does the same.\n   - Fix: drop the noqa and comment why the import is needed, or wrap the currency call so that an exception keeps status=mismatch.\n5. P2 — templates/settings/settings.user.json:149.\n   - Problem: the evidence pointer `.claude/hooks/check_pair_rail.py:157-169,1502-1511` points into a file that now has 216 lines.\n   - Fix: repoint it to _lib/_pair_rail_parts/part_01.py and part_03.py.\n6. P2 — .claude/scripts/_restore_archive.py:99-104 against .claude/scripts/ceo-backup.sh:262-265.\n   - Problem: `--include-plans` uses `cp -pR`, which keeps symlinks found under .claude/plans, while the restore validator refuses any link member.\n   - Scenario: such a backup is created successfully and then cannot be restored. This is fail-closed, so no data is lost.\n   - Fix: copy only regular files for plans as well, as the memory/ copy already does, or warn when the backup is made.\n7. P2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_precompact_parts/__init__.py:16.\n   - Problem: exec'ing parts that start with a docstring overwrites the facade's module __doc__ with the last part's docstring (\"PreCompact hook dispatch…\"). No production code reads it.\n   - Fix: remove the part docstrings, or restore __doc__ after install.\n8. P2 — _restore_archive.py:122-136.\n   - Problem: complete_members relies on TarFile.fileobj and TarFile.offset, which are internal attributes. They are stable on 3.9-3.14, but nothing pins that.\n   - Fix: add a test on every interpreter in the matrix (tests are out of scope here).","decision":"GO","sentence":"The declared conditions this payload touches (5, 7, 9 and 10) hold against the code, the moved pair-rail and precompact code keeps its names, patch points and fail-open direction, and the remaining findings are P2 follow-ups with no P0."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1611,"cache_read_input_tokens":250018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1611},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a4f4d70-7bb8-4cdc-868c-8f5f354648e0","uuid":"404ad845-3621-4fb0-a385-2fe640418dd5","timestamp":"2026-11-15T11:09:15.300Z","request_id":"req_011Ch4cFMb32HsGqKpD5dHeM","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Sr2MdsQX2UKKtXuAmsD6n3":{"report":"PAYLOAD 23/32 — check_pair_rail.py → facade over _lib/_pair_rail_parts; check_plan_edit.py → _lib/plan_paths; check_precompact_continuity.py → facade over _lib/_precompact_parts; new _contamination_inventory.py, _repin_guard.py, _restore_archive.py, _subprocess_census.py; raw docstring in architect-bundle-validate.py.\n\nDECLARED CONDITIONS CHECKED AGAINST THE CODE IN THIS PAYLOAD (all true)\n- C5: